From dfd4f3dbbfed148105d54418e31a2a91b7955654 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert DeLanghe <1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:21:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(convo,pi): who served the model rides the RFC's actor
 slot; pi keeps its provider across a round trip
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Turn gains `provider: Option<String>` (who served `model`: anthropic,
openai, ollama …). derive writes it to meta.actors["agent:<model>"].provider,
the slot RFC.md and the kind spec already name for it; extract reads it
back. Before, derive filled that slot with the harness name ("pi",
"claude-code"), which duplicates meta.source and inverts the RFC's own
example; extract ignores such legacy values.

pi's reader now keeps each assistant message's provider and its writer
prefers it over the "anthropic" default, so ollama/gemma4 comes back as
ollama/gemma4 (test provider_survives_round_trip). The stale Turn.extra
paragraphs in the pi and codex writer headers are replaced with what the
code does (Turn has no extras; codex's encrypted reasoning and tool
extras are not round-tripped).

Snapshots: document@* lose the harness value under agent actors (pi
gains "ollama"); ir@pi gains provider per turn; 32 cross-harness
round_trip snapshots list meta.actors.<actor>.provider as lost — the key
path now only exists on non-agent actors in the source.
